From: BasaltVR build <build@basaltvr.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: force Unity OpenXR multipass for 2D IOSurface swapchains

Basalt's native handoff intentionally exposes one simple IOSurface-backed 2D
swapchain per eye and rejects texture arrays. If DXMT advertises
VPAndRTArrayIndexFromAnyShaderFeedingRasterizer, Unity retains Single Pass
Instanced shaders after the array swapchain rejection. Eye-indexed fullscreen
lighting and fog then render in only one eye.

Report the capability conservatively. Unity's OpenXR provider consequently
uses its documented multipass fallback, matching Basalt's independent 2D eye
surfaces.
---
 src/d3d11/d3d11_inspection.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_inspection.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_inspection.cpp
index be6c235..0380508 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_inspection.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_inspection.cpp
@@ -59,7 +59,17 @@ MTLD3D11Device::MTLD3D11Device() {
   m_d3d11Options.OutputMergerLogicOp = TRUE;
 #endif
 
-  m_d3d11Options3.VPAndRTArrayIndexFromAnyShaderFeedingRasterizer = TRUE;
+  /*
+   * Basalt exports simple IOSurface-backed 2D swapchains and deliberately
+   * rejects texture-array OpenXR swapchains. Advertising arbitrary-stage
+   * render-target-array indexing makes Unity keep Single Pass Instanced
+   * shaders even after that rejection. Full-screen lighting and fog passes
+   * then receive a valid stereo eye index only for one eye.
+   *
+   * Report the capability conservatively so Unity's OpenXR provider selects
+   * its supported multipass path, with one independent draw per eye.
+   */
+  m_d3d11Options3.VPAndRTArrayIndexFromAnyShaderFeedingRasterizer = FALSE;
 
   m_d3d11Options5.SharedResourceTier = D3D11_SHARED_RESOURCE_TIER_0; // TODO
 
-- 
